{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/337192-building-a-sidereal-crime-lord","id":337192,"title":"Building a Sidereal Crime Lord","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-11T10:49:05-08:00","id":337192,"title":"Building a Sidereal Crime Lord","content":"I was wondering if anyone had any tips for putting together a Sidereal criminal mastermind.<br /> <br /> The basic idea is that &quot;Uncle&quot; Lo Chen was a low-level functionary in some syndicate when he exalted almost a thousand years ago. On being whisked away to Heaven, he quickly realized that the same methods of how the underworld works, how to gain power and keep it, applied to the Gods there; only the goods and services were different, and being a Vizier gave him prime access to them.<br /> <br /> The Contagion was a godsend to Uncle's business, as it resulted in tons of newly destitute deities now in need of his discreet aid. Lo Chen still makes sure to publicly attend all the duties expected of a Seer, including Convention work, but it all takes a backseat to his true, lucrative, passion.<br /> <br /> Of course, Uncle was not the first Sidereal to have these goals and methods, nor the last, but he has proven the most successful, buying out/eliminating his older rivals, and incorporating the younger ones into his organization. Privately, he denounces both Gold and Bronze Factions as idealistic fools, and he only has slightly more respect for the pragmatic Independents. However, Lo Chen happily accepts interviews from all Seers, most of whom hear rumors of his influence and come to him for help, which he is glad to provide for favors, to be named later, if ever.<br /> <br /> Gods also come to Uncle for help, whether for aid in swaying the bureaucracy of Yu-Shan or for Astrological Blessings and Curses, which he sells at a premium (his influence is also good for assuring another Sidereal's Astrological petition quickly gets the many co-signatures it needs). Uncle lives well above his actual Salary grade, in the best manses that the Celestial City has to offer. However, he headquarters his business in the Empty Quarters of Yu-Shan, where his Sidereal and godly lieutenants sell prayers, mortal slaves, even new domains for gods to represent.<br /> <br /> Shining Barrator utterly despises Uncle, and lists taking him and his organization down as one of his top missions in life...but even if he were to succeed, it would be unlikely if the Elemental Dragon judge at his trial would do more than give him a slap on the wrist, maybe a century in the more pleasant side of the Archipelago of the Exiles, nowhere near the Gaol of Roaring Thunder...<br /> <br /> Ok, that's all I've got so far. Any ideas or advice? Maybe he should be younger? And what Caste does this sound like?<br /> <br /> Any particular Charm usage he should specialize in? What are some Artifacts/Martial Arts that sound like they'd fit this NPC, if any? Any ideas for associates, enemies, rivals, or other plot hooks? (A moll, he needs a moll...)<br /> <br /> Any help or suggestions is greatly appreciated!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 12-11-2014, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T10:57:20-08:00","id":337216,"title":"","content":"I don't have much to add, but I love this character concept. I always wanted to play around with the Slums of Yu-Shan. One concept I had was a Slum Fight Club. All that paper pushing and red tape must build up a lot of frustrations and it would be nice to have a way to vent them. The sort of place where High Level Gods and Sidereals can go and kick the crap out of each other. Or bet on the fights, if the player isn't combat oriented. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T11:03:22-08:00","id":337218,"title":"","content":"Ooh, good one, hadn't thought of that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, he charges for access to an arena featuring combat between gods, mortals, god-blooded...even the odd Deiphage that they manage to capture! <br /> <br /> Thanks!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T11:06:14-08:00","id":337221,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that before you think about Charms, think about other traits that a crime lord would have. High Intelligence, Wits and Charisma and/or Manipulation. Abilities like Larceny, Awareness, Investigation (mostly to know how to to throw authorities off his trail and to create reasons to throw suspicion on others), Socialize, Lore (some great prediction stuff in there) and probably Stealth, plus Dodge and Occult of course. Does he appear to be the kindly old uncle on top of a giant web of more powerful minions? Then Performance; if he's clearly a badass top dog, then Presence. Maybe War to coordinate all his minions if needed but that seems secondary.<br /> <br /> Sounds like a Chosen of Secrets to me but I could also see him as a Joybringer - after all, he's improving so many lives with his actions, who cares if they're outside the law! <br /> <br /> In terms of MA and with the experience of 1000 years, you want to specialize in things like Black Claw Style (it makes anyone coming down on him look overzealous or bullying) and White Veil (super secretive attacks and powers). Focus on things like this - abilities that are subtle, that you might be able to slip a debilitating Charm into a Combo for that extra oomph or deliver what appears to be a mundane blow that actually does a lot more nasty stuff than you might think. He probably would know a more popular Style to exhibit on missions or in public and something like Crane or Crystal Chameleon seem like they'd fit the character. This would probably go well with SMA like Charcoal March of Spiders, and there's little reason a millennium-old Sid would not be invested in Prismatic Arrangement of Creation (as it's said to be a Style that most Sidereals are taught). I like Quicksilver Hand of Dreams thematically to pursue rivals and possible minions into their dreams to convince them and it definitely plays up the &quot;you can never get away&quot; aspect of a syndicate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T11:24:48-08:00","id":337233,"title":"","content":"Excellent ideas, Z! Yeah, he's definitely the &quot;kindly old uncle&quot; looking type, very affable and avuncular.<br /> <br /> I'm leaning more to Chosen of Serenity, rather than Secrets; both anima powers could be useful, but the Joybringer one would be more useful for his Astrological shenanigans. Speaking of which, any Resplendencies that are recommended?<br /> <br /> I'm definitely giving him Throne Shadow style, but BC and WV sound appropriate as well. I want to give him one of the Four Arguments of Virtue styles, which one sounds most fitting? <br /> <br /> Also, any particular Spells that he should know?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T11:49:50-08:00","id":337286,"title":"","content":"Oh, also look into...maybe First Pulse fits thematically for him too? Not sure if it fits your vision. As to Virtue Styles, he sounds very much like his primary Virtue is Conviction and that he might have a lower Compassion and Temperance (I'd think that higher Temperance might be tied to being more likely to follow the law). IIRC the Conviction style is not an optimized style (lacks a perfect) but if you want cheap perfects, you have Crane for that. :P<br /> <br /> If he's &quot;kindly old uncle&quot; I'd go with Performance over Presence. Serenity will definitely benefit from this. <br /> <br /> Spells...here are some suggestions.<br /> <br /> TCS: Coin of Distant Vision, Corrupted Words, Droning Suggestion, Open the Spirit Door, Peacock Shadow Eyes<br /> CCS: Cloud Trapeze, Hidden Judges of the Secret Flame, Insidious Tendrils of Hate, Summon the Heavenly Portal, Threefold Binding of the Heart, Whirlwind of Fate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T16:03:30-08:00","id":337472,"title":"","content":"Sidereal Socialize seems like the keystone for a mob boss sidereal, and I think he probably works best as a Serenity, so that's a good place to start. It's extremely effective at exploiting social relationships, and mostly keeps your fingerprints off it. Cash and Murder Games and Wanting and Fearing Prayer are highly desirable for a Godfather figure, and Life Without Compunction helps if you get called out.<br /> <br /> Performance is good for being liked, but it also has some very effective levers for messing with gods in Song of Spirit Persuasion and Ice and Fire Binding (which works on all spirits as of 2.5, and can compel a spirit to protect &quot;a social group&quot;, which probably covers a sufficiently large crime syndicate).<br /> <br /> Bureaucracy would be my number three pick: Terminal Sanction seems like this guy's jam, and Icy Hand makes him effective as a &quot;fixer&quot; and can help keep people in line in your own syndicate (though be cautious about this, since it can cause problems in an organization that exists to support its founder). Underling Invisibility Practice might also be useful for playing someone who seems innocuous but is actually a mastermind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T07:37:25-08:00","id":338061,"title":"","content":"Ditto Gayo; that's basically what I'd do. Presence has a few good Charms too, though: Force Decision is good for getting people to do what you want and Impose Motivation is great for someone who has a strong Motivation and wants underlings to carry it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}